Hi all,

 

I am running BlueZ 3.32 protocol stack on the embedded ARM-based platform on
the linux-2.6.10 kernel. 

 

I am using ttyCPM2 serial interface at the 500000 baud rate as the HCI
interface to BlueCore module (BC04) attached to the BlueZ upper layer stack.

I am using this script:

 

dbus-daemon --system

hciattach -s 500000 /dev/ttyCPM2 bcsp 500000 noflow

hciconfig hci0 up

hcid -d -f /etc/bluetooth/hcid.conf 

sdpd

pand --listen --role GN --master --autozap --devup /etc/bluetooth/pan/dev-up

brctl addbr pan0

ifconfig pan0 192.168.2.1

brctl setfd pan0 0

brctl stp pan0 disable

 

I created successfully PAN-profile bluetooth access point. 

Generally all basic fuctionality seems to be OK i.e. BNEP interface get
created successfully and the access to LAN is working fine.

 

The problem is triggered when I try to increase the traffic via the HCI bcsp
link between ARM processor and BC04 for example when I try to make a ftp
connection trought 

my embedded linux device running bluez and my laptop.

In particular when the traffic is ARM->BC04 direction, data transfer works
fine, instead when the traffic is BC04->ARM direction 

but I receive these messages that destroy my ftp application:

 

bcsp_recv: Out-of-order packet arrived, got 1 expected 4

 

Somebody could help me?

 

Thank you in advance.



Best regards. 

 

Gianluigi


